WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.488
In Xia's final years, King Jie had lost the support of many people.

00:00:07.838 --> 00:00:11.390
The people suffered, and the lords were deeply disappointed in Jie.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:16.348
Tang, leader of the Shang tribe, was a wise and worthy ruler.

00:00:16.698 --> 00:00:20.346
He cared for the people, and many came to join him.

00:00:20.696 --> 00:00:24.944
Growing stronger, Tang united the strength of other tribes.

00:00:25.294 --> 00:00:28.846
Together they resolved to rise against the cruel Jie.

00:00:29.196 --> 00:00:33.876
Tang led the allied army out, and people lined the road to see them off.

00:00:34.226 --> 00:00:38.210
The allies' morale was high, and they advanced unstoppably, like a knife through bamboo.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:42.856
At the Battle of Mingtiao, Tang defeated Jie's army.

00:00:43.206 --> 00:00:48.030
Jie fled, and the rule of the Xia dynasty came to an end.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:52.196
Tang founded the Shang dynasty and opened a new era.

00:00:52.546 --> 00:00:59.506
This story shows that a ruler who loses the people's hearts will lose the realm.

